+## [3.1.0] - 2026-07-31
+
+### Added
+- Custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint support through `NEXUS_OPENAI_BASE_URL`,
+  `NEXUS_OPENAI_API_KEY`, and `--model custom --model-id ...`.
+- Shared backend preflight diagnostics for the CLI, doctor, and benchmark runner.
+- Explicit `--local-intern {off,auto,required}`, `--enable-nova-fallback`, and
+  `--enable-plugins` controls.
+- Structured benchmark failure phases, types, environment classification, and
+  redacted stdout/stderr tails.
+- Source-checkout OpenAI-compatible HTTP fallback when the official SDK has not
+  yet been installed.
+
+### Changed
+- Nova is optional for hosted coding runs. Hosted models execute directly when
+  a local intern is disabled or unavailable.
+- OpenRouter uses the requested/configured model instead of silently replacing
+  it with a hard-coded fallback model.
+- Budget accounting now estimates token usage when a provider omits usage data.
+- Project and checkout `.env` files now match the documented loading behavior.
+- Generated runtime/evaluation evidence is excluded from source releases to avoid
+  publishing machine-specific paths or repository content.
+- Version bumped to 3.1.0 with 243 deterministic tests.
+
+### Security
+- `web_fetch` now enforces scheme, DNS/IP-range, content-type, response-size,
+  and redirect policy checks to reduce SSRF and local-network exposure.
+
 ## [3.0.0] - 2026-07-29
 
 Single integrated Nexus software-engineering runtime.
